# Code owners for the EDW Flyway repository (Bitbucket Cloud).
#
# PLACE THIS FILE AT .bitbucket/CODEOWNERS in the EDW repository (the root of the copied kit). It is kept under
# bitbucket/ in the kit only so that it is reviewed together with the branch restrictions.
#
# Format: one rule per line, `<path pattern> <owner> [<owner> ...]`; `#` starts a comment. Patterns follow
# .gitignore rules (a trailing / means "everything below"; a pattern with a / in the middle is relative to the repo
# root). Owners are Bitbucket groups written @<workspace>/<group-slug> (or individual users). Replace `alfa` with the
# real workspace slug and create the groups under Workspace settings > User groups before the first pull request.
# Rules are ordered general -> specific: the later, more specific line is the one that should decide a file, as in
# GitHub's CODEOWNERS (verify the precedence on the first pull request that touches migrations/SALES/).
# Reviewer selection can be narrowed per group, e.g. `@alfa/edw-dba:random(1)` -- verify the selector syntax first.
#
# ENFORCEMENT CAVEAT: Bitbucket Cloud uses this file to SUGGEST / add code owners as reviewers; on its own it does
# not stop a merge. Blocking on owner approval needs a merge check, and enforced merge checks need Bitbucket Premium
# (unverified, confirm on the workspace's plan). The API has a `require_review_group_approvals_to_merge` restriction
# kind whose exact semantics are undocumented; the alternative is a Marketplace code-owners app. What IS enforced
# without it: two approvals, one default-reviewer approval and a green Jenkins build
# (bitbucket/branch-restrictions.json, applied by bitbucket/apply_branch_restrictions.sh).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- catch-all: DBA review for anything unowned
*                                   @alfa/edw-dba

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- database code: schema owners + DBA
# One pair of lines per schema folder. Keep @alfa/edw-dba on every SQL rule: a later, more specific rule replaces
# the catch-all instead of adding to it.
migrations/                         @alfa/edw-dba
repeatable/                         @alfa/edw-dba
migrations/SALES/                   @alfa/edw-sales @alfa/edw-dba
repeatable/SALES/                   @alfa/edw-sales @alfa/edw-dba
migrations/FINANCE/                 @alfa/edw-finance @alfa/edw-dba
repeatable/FINANCE/                 @alfa/edw-finance @alfa/edw-dba

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- platform: runs on every deploy to every runway
# Callbacks and the Flyway / runway configuration change the behaviour of every deploy; the CI/CD code holds the
# approval, lock and promotion gates; bootstrap/ holds the Snowflake account objects and grants.
callbacks/                          @alfa/edw-platform
flyway.toml                         @alfa/edw-platform
runways.toml                        @alfa/edw-platform
sqlfluff.cfg                        @alfa/edw-platform
rules/                              @alfa/edw-platform
scripts/                            @alfa/edw-platform
jenkins/                            @alfa/edw-platform
bootstrap/                          @alfa/edw-platform @alfa/edw-dba
bitbucket/                          @alfa/edw-platform
.bitbucket/                         @alfa/edw-platform
docs/                               @alfa/edw-platform
README.md                           @alfa/edw-platform
